   "text": {
    "L1": "Rectangles can look different but cover the same number of square tiles.",
    "L2": "A longer shape does not always have more area. Area counts the tiles inside.",
    "L3": "With 12 tiles, the side pairs are 1 by 12, 2 by 6, and 3 by 4.",
    "L4": "Each pair multiplies to 12, so all three rectangles have the same area.",
    "L5": "Their perimeters differ: the 1 by 12 boundary is 26 units, while the 3 by 4 boundary is 14 units.",
    "L6": "A long thin shape has more tile edges on the outside. A compact shape shares more edges inside.",
    "L7": "For area 20, the pairs are 1 by 20, 2 by 10, and 4 by 5.",
    "L8": "The squarest rectangle, 4 by 5, has the shortest boundary. Now choose the 12-tile rectangle with the shortest boundary."
   },
